        "title": {
          "en": "Enterprise AI Focus Shifts to Operating Layer Ownership",
          "zh": "企业级AI焦点转向运营层所有权"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "While public discourse tracks foundation models, the practical advantage in enterprise AI is shifting to ownership of the operating layer that governs and improves AI applications.",
          "zh": "尽管公众讨论仍关注基础模型，但企业级AI的实际优势正转向AI应用所用、治理和改进的运营层的所有权。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "Public discourse regarding enterprise AI primarily focuses on foundation models and benchmarks.",
            "Specific topics of public conversation include comparisons like \"GPT versus Gemini,\" analysis of \"reasoning scores,\" and \"marginal capability gains.\"",
            "A more durable advantage in enterprise AI is structural, derived from owning the operating layer where intelligence is applied, governed, and improved."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "关于企业级AI的公众讨论主要关注基础模型和基准测试。",
            "公众关注的具体话题包括GPT与Gemini等模型间的比较、推理分数分析以及边际能力提升。",
            "企业级AI更持久的优势在于结构性，源于对AI应用、治理和改进的运营层的所有权。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "This shift indicates that long-term value in enterprise AI may increasingly derive from infrastructure controlling AI application and governance, rather than solely from foundational model capabilities. Companies may gain competitive advantages by developing or acquiring ownership of this critical operating layer.",
          "zh": "这一转变表明，企业级AI的长期价值可能越来越多地来源于控制AI应用和治理的基础设施，而不仅仅是基础模型能力。公司可通过开发或获得这一关键运营层的所有权来获得竞争优势。"
        },
        "source": "MIT Tech Review (AI)",
        "link": "https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/04/16/1135554/treating-enterprise-ai-as-an-operating-layer/"
